// A pair piped into a two-parameter function REFUSES (E_TypeMismatch —
// the function-arity face): the parameter lists pair arity for arity, and
// this program's do not. Until 2026-09-27 a unification rule decomposed the
// single tuple against the two parameters ("parameters ARE tuples") and
// the program checked clean — then trapped at the indirect call, because
// the emit never carried that rule into the calling convention. Measured
// RED-first on boot b145b836: exit 0, no diagnostic, `indirect call type
// mismatch` at run. The capability this refusal names is
// `Hβ.lower.parameter-product-calling-convention`; this file turns green
// only by that landing, never by re-admitting the shape at the type layer.
fn add(a, b) = a + b

fn main() = (1, 2) |> add
